WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.610
Dominance is a phenomenon in which one allele

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.660
masks the effect of the other.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.480
That’s how we understand it.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.471
But we have also learned that in some cases,

00:00:15.471 --> 00:00:18.520
a dominant allele does not completely supress

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.630
the recessive one.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.392
The blend of both the genes is seen with an

00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:24.870
intermediate phenotype.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.360
And what if both the different genes are dominant?

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.831
In such exceptional cases, an individual with

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.300
both the phenotypes is obtained.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.500
We have learned all the three types of Dominance

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.630
so far!

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:43.140
Let us do a quick review of all the 3 types.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.880
Firstly, can you tell me what Dominance is?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.237
Technically, it can be defined as the relation

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.960
between two alleles of a gene and the associated

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.160
phenotype.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.940
That means, dominance is all about how one

00:00:57.942 --> 00:01:01.230
dominant allele of a particular gene interacts

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.040
with the other recessive or dominant allele

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.680
of the same gene set in an organism.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.600
So if “T” is one allele from a gene set

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.270
which is dominant for the trait “height”,

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:15.840
then its effect on the other allele, which

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.520
may be “t” or “T”, is called Dominance!

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.620
Based on the gene interactions, Dominance

00:01:23.627 --> 00:01:26.270
is categorised into three types.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.399
Complete Dominance which is very common in nature.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.500
And Incomplete and Codominance which are relatively

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.020
rare.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.697
Let us review all these three types with one

00:01:36.697 --> 00:01:38.869
common and simple example.

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:42.391
We can hypothetically take the alleles “capital

00:01:42.391 --> 00:01:45.689
B” and “lower case w” to represent different

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.729
flower colours.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:50.100
Let “B” be the allele for flower colour

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.300
blue which we consider as dominant.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.722
The allele for white flowers which will be

00:01:55.722 --> 00:01:58.249
a recessive trait will be represented by the

00:01:58.249 --> 00:02:01.229
letter “w” in lower case.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:04.338
So the genotype of the plant with blue flowers

00:02:04.338 --> 00:02:07.109
will be “BB” in capital and that of white

00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:10.460
flowered plant will be “ww” in lower case

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:14.000
considering both are homozygous!

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.040
The first type in the list is complete dominance.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.623
Here, the dominant allele will mask the effect

00:02:20.623 --> 00:02:23.350
of the recessive allele completely!

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.320
So on crossing the blue and white flowered

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.960
plants, we will obtain only blue coloured

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.360
flowers.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.020
To be precise, on crossing the two homozygous

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:38.300
varieties, we will get all heterozygous offsprings.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.477
Now this being a case of complete dominance,

00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:44.860
all the plants will have blue coloured flowers.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.460
Can you state an example of complete dominance

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.600
found in nature?

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.620
Most of the dominant traits fall under this category.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.636
For example, the purple colour of flowers,

00:02:56.636 --> 00:02:59.580
axial flower position, tall height of the

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.307
plant, all these characters found in a pea

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:04.970
plant fall under the category of complete

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.080
dominance!

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.470
Next in the list is incomplete dominance.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.420
In this type, the dominant allele masks the

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.220
effect of the recessive one, but not completely.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.600
That means a phenotype which is intermediate

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.700
of the two parents is obtained in the F1 hybrid!

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:28.460
Any guesses what will happen in this case?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.931
If this is a case of incomplete dominance,

00:03:30.931 --> 00:03:33.520
then an intermediate of the two colours will

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.670
be obtained.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.360
Maybe light blue colour.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.147
Theoretically, “BB” crossed with “ww”

00:03:42.147 --> 00:03:43.990
will give us “Bw”.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.480
So genotypically all the F1 hybrids will have

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.820
both the alleles.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.740
Phenotypically, all these offsprings will

00:03:51.748 --> 00:03:54.490
have an intermediate colour between dark blue

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.540
and white!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.626
In nature, incomplete dominance is seen in

00:03:59.626 --> 00:04:02.050
plants like the 4o’ clock plants.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.560
In humans, we have seen that incomplete dominance

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.600
is seen in hair type.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:10.030
Curly hair, which is a dominant trait when

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.680
crossed with straight hair that is a recessive

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:16.350
trait, gives us wavy hair.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.056
Wavy hair is a trait intermediate of both

00:04:19.056 --> 00:04:22.159
the types and hence is an example of INCOMPLETE

00:04:22.159 --> 00:04:24.389
dominance!

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:26.900
Now comes the third type, which is called

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:27.960
Codominance!

00:04:27.969 --> 00:04:30.988
Let us assume we have another dominant allele

00:04:30.988 --> 00:04:33.000
for the “red coloured flower”.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.300
So the genotype of a plant with this coloured

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.740
flower will be “RR”.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.194
Any idea what will happen if this plant is

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.160
crossed with the one having blue coloured

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.240
flowers?

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.420
Both “Red” and “Blue” coloured flowers

00:04:47.427 --> 00:04:48.710
are dominant traits.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:51.261
So both the alleles will try getting expressed

00:04:51.261 --> 00:04:52.360
with equal strength.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.912
As a result, we will obtain a progeny that

00:04:55.912 --> 00:04:59.539
has either blue flowers with red patches or

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:02.620
red flowers with blue patches!

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.657
That means both blue and red colours will

00:05:05.657 --> 00:05:07.360
be seen in the flowers!

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.431
Theoretically, the cross of “RR” and “BB”

00:05:11.431 --> 00:05:15.900
will yield F1 hybrids with the genotype “RB”.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.800
As a result, flowers having petals with both

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.279
colors will be obtained!

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:25.669
Codominance is found widely in nature!

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:28.634
Most common examples of Codominance that we

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:31.599
have learnt include the human blood groups,

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:36.060
coat colour in cattle and in many other animals.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.028
Mendelism revolves around complete dominance,

00:05:39.028 --> 00:05:41.930
as it doesn’t favour blending of characters.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:45.242
Hence, the other two types: Incomplete and

00:05:45.242 --> 00:05:48.949
Codominance, are commonly studied as exceptions

00:05:48.949 --> 00:05:49.899
to Mendelism.

